The measurements index published `<=25.0%` for the one quantity a program-level
decision band is written against ("<=25% useful => recall stays stopped"). That
figure was not derivable from the record: it was added a day after 0006, in the
commit that published 0008, and 0006's body names exactly five vacuous TPs,
which supports 29.5%.

Re-derived under ADR-0046's two named classes over 0006's own ledger:
27 useful of 112 adjudicated = 24.1%, with 11 KIND-MISDECLARED and
0 CONFIGURED-ACTION. Correctness precision is untouched at 33.9%. The bound
survives; the derivation did not. `gibom_08272026/derive.py` recomputes every
figure from ledger-final.json and pass4-summary.json, so no count is
hand-copied.

CONFIGURED-ACTION contributing zero refutes the expectation ADR-0046 itself
recorded. The reason is structural, not luck: 0006's claim set admits only
env_read and host_info_read sources, so clause 2 -- deserialization into a type
whose fields are declared as a configuration schema -- has no candidate. The
ADR's motivating shape (caddy) belongs to 0005's cohort. Nearest miss
disclosed: cilium reads os.Getenv(SockPathEnv) and dials the socket it names;
clauses 1 and 3 cite, clause 2 does not, so it counts useful.

Six of the eleven deductions are a bash defect section A named only in part --
`>` redirects whose every target is /dev/null, cited to the line, fixed the
next day by PR #541. The other five are shellcheck's Haskell IORef/STRef under
db_read, which haskell.yaml's own boundary_ruling: unruled note already calls
"in-process mutable references, not a database".

One reversal recorded: gocryptfs was first labelled discard-only on four
/dev/null sites; a raw re-read found a fifth, `exec 200> "$LOCKFILE"`, whose
path is env-derived (TMPDIR -> TESTDIR -> LOCKFILE). A genuine environment-to-
filesystem write. The first cut would have published 23.2%.

Two of section A's own rows are struck rather than carried -- INV-nular's
reproduction refuted ">&2 counts" and ">> reported as >". Conversely, argv and
application-config under env_read are documented deliberate rows awaiting a
vocabulary ruling, so they are published as sensitivities with arithmetic
(15.2% / 19.6% / 21.4%, and 10.7% if all resolve against) rather than deducted.
Two new sink-side defects found in passing (io_lib:format declared logging;
urllib.request.Request declared net_send though it is a constructor) go to
INV-nular.

